<http://data.silknow.org/object/7beaefb0-48a4-3482-8195-c580f92bd2a5>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Circular mat for a<i> huqqa</i> pipe, or tray cover, the ground is made of flattened gold wire, over which are applied a central field with floral designs in gold-wrapped thread and sequins, surrounded by a band of flowers made up of red and green spangles on a fringe of flattened gold wire. With a single central floral motif, composed of gold sequins and gold-wrapped thread. Backed with crimson silk."@en , "Textile, tray cover or <i>huqqa</i> mat, silk, gold wire, applied gold-wrapped thread, Madras, ca. 1855"@en , "Intended for use as a mat for placing a <i>huqqa</i> pipe on, or as a tray cover."@en ;
